(6450882, 956928, 104518, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the quote. I have just ordered The Collected Works of Wallace Stevens. I suspect the symbolism suffered from the audience''s ignorance, like mine. The photo is certainly striking enough.<br/> <br/>I am struggling with the knife, since<br/>"This luscious and impeccable fruit of life<br/>Falls, it appears, of its own weight to earth."<br/> <br/>I suppose the knife is a supporting symbolism of death, but a violent one?</td>', 'Thank you for the quote. I have just ordered The Collected Works of Wallace Stevens. I suspect the symbolism suffered from the audience''s ignorance, like mine. The photo is certainly striking enough. I am struggling with the knife, since"This luscious and impeccable fruit of lifeFalls, it appears, of its own weight to earth." I suppose the knife is a supporting symbolism of death, but a violent one?', '2011-06-23 10:15:21.000000', NULL, 0),
