(6451937, 956714, 49683, '<td valign="top">The still life symbolism is to Cancer.  It affects us all, in one way or another.  Fathers, Mothers and Children.  Letting go, leaves you hallow inside, thus the hallow shells, a piece of you gone forever.  The claw is to symbolizes a grip that we have on life.  The soft out of focus whiter sand infront represents the letting go of life, something even a crabs strong grip cannot hold.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-24 16:35:00.</i></td>', 'The still life symbolism is to Cancer.  It affects us all, in one way or another.  Fathers, Mothers and Children.  Letting go, leaves you hallow inside, thus the hallow shells, a piece of you gone forever.  The claw is to symbolizes a grip that we have on life.  The soft out of focus whiter sand infront represents the letting go of life, something even a crabs strong grip cannot hold.', '2011-06-24 17:30:06.000000', '2011-06-24 17:35:00.000000', 0),
